      "scene_id": "scene_0",
      "purpose": "Show scan progressing through candidates",
      "start_ms": 6000,
      "end_ms": 14000
    },
    {
      "text": "An index instead maps a search key to matching rows, so the lookup need not test every row.",
      "evidence": {
        "source_id": "src_storyboard",
        "segment_ids": [
          "seg_lookup"
        ],
        "start_ms": null,
        "end_ms": null,
        "quote": "A table scan tests rows to find matching data. An index maps keys to rows and can find matching entries without testing every row. An index takes storage space and must be updated when indexed values change."
      },
